:\n56|         \"\"\"Called when the parser leaves the element.\n57| \n58|         Args:\n59|             context (MarkdownContext): [description]\n60|         \"\"\"\n61| \n62|     def on_child_close(self, context: MarkdownContext, child: MarkdownElement) -> bool:\n63|         \"\"\"Called when \n[... observation truncated ...]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_rich_3942.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for rich_3942 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom rich.default_styles import __rich_console__  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# Update to markdown styles Updates to Markdown styling\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", __rich_console__)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "rich_3942", "repo": "Textualize/rich", "base_commit": "c595fa95068dd2c5095d25446b2f0571bc0b3995", "files": ["rich/default_styles.py", "rich/markdown.py"], "symbols": ["__rich_console__", "HeadingFormat", "Heading", "create"], "n_hunks": 7, "n_files": 2, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/_card_render.py", "tests/test_markdown.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 18, "generat