d>false</StorageEncrypted>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The `VpcSecurityGroups` section in the XML response template is correctly set up to iterate over `cluster.vpc_security_groups` and include each security group ID. Since the `vpc_security_groups` attribute is now correctly populated in the `Cluster` class, the response should reflect this.\n\nLet's rerun the script to verify if the changes are now correctly reflected in the response.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python3 /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1/reproduce_error.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [execute_bash]:\npython3 /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1/reproduce_error.py\r\nVpcSecurityGroups: [][Python Interpreter: /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/bin/python]\nroot@openhands-workspace:/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1 # \n[Command finished with exit code 0]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The `VpcSecurityGroups` field is still empty, indicating that the changes are not being reflected in the response. Let's ensure that the `vpc_security_group_ids` are correctly passed and processed throughout the code.\n\nI'll review the flow of data from the request to the response to identify any missing links or errors. Let's check the code where the `create_db_cluster` method is called and ensure that the `vpc_security_group_ids` are included in the `kwargs` dictionary.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"grep -n 'create_db_cluster' /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1/moto/rds/responses.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [execute_bash]:\ngrep -n 'create_db_cluster' /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1/moto/rds/responses.py\r\n35:        if name in [\"create_db_cluster\", \"create_global_cluster\"]:\r\n598:    def create_db_cluster(self) -> str:\r\n600:        cluster = self.backend.create_db_cluster(kwargs)\r\n641:    def create_db_cluster_snapshot(self) -> str:\r\n645:  