the fix works by:\n   - Creating and running a reproduction script that matches the PR's test case\n   - Confirming we now get the proper error message: \"An error occurred (DBClusterNotFoundFault) when calling the DescribeDBClusters operation: DBCluster clustername not found\"\n   - Considering edge cases which are all handled appropriately\n\n4. The implementation follows the pattern used in similar methods in the codebase, like `delete_db_cluster_snapshot` which also checks existence before accessing the dictionary.\n\nThe fix is complete and working as expected. I'll finish the interaction now.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"submit_patch\", \"arguments\": {}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "swegym-sft", "instance_id": "getmoto__moto__3.1", "traj_turn": 10, "tool": "submit_patch", "est_tokens": 1580}}
