ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\u2728 Add support for Server Sent Events\n\n\u2728 Add support for Server Sent Events\r\n\r\nThis will be available in FastAPI 0.135.0, released in the next hours."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/openapi/utils.py (hunk at line 29).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"from fastapi.openapi.models import OpenAPI\\nfrom fastapi.params import Body, ParamTypes\\nfrom fastapi.responses import Response\\nfrom fastapi.types import ModelNameMap\\nfrom fastapi.utils import (\\n    deep_dict_update,\", \"new_text\": \"from fastapi.openapi.models import OpenAPI\\nfrom fastapi.params import Body, ParamTypes\\nfrom fastapi.responses import Response\\nfrom fastapi.sse import _SSE_EVENT_SCHEMA\\nfrom fastapi.types import ModelNameMap\\nfrom fastapi.utils import (\\n    deep_dict_update,\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/openapi/utils.py (hunk at line 373).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"                    operation.setdefault(\\\"responses\\\", {}).setdefault(\\n                        status_code, {}\\n                    ).setdefault(\\\"content\\\", {})[\\\"application/jsonl\\\"] = jsonl_content\\n                elif route_response_media_type:\\n                    response_schema = {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}\\n                    if lenient_issubclass(current_response_class, JSONResponse):\", \"new_text\": \"                    operation.setdefault(\\\"responses\\\", {}).setdefault(\\n                        status_code, {}\\n                    ).setdefault(\\\"content\\\", {})[\\\"application/jsonl\\\"] = jsonl_content\\n                elif route.is_sse_stream:\\n                    sse_content: dict[str, Any] = {}\\n                    item_schema = copy.deepcopy(_SSE_EVENT_SCHEMA)\\n                    if route.stream_item_field:\\n                        content_schema = get_schema_from_model_field(\\n                            field=route.stream_item_field,\\n                            model_name_map=model_name_map,\\n                            field_mapping=field_mapping,\\n                            separate_input_output_schemas=separate_input_output_schemas,\\n                        )\\n                        item_schema[\\\"required\\\"] = [\\\"data\\\"]\\n                        item_schema[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"data\\\"] = {\\n                            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                            \\\"contentMediaType\\\": \\\"application/json\\\",\\n                            \\\"contentSchema\\\": content_schema,\\n                        }\\n                    sse_content[\\\"itemSchema\\\"] = item_schema\\n                    operation.setdefault(\\\"responses\\\", {}).setdefault(\\n                        status_code, {}\\n                    ).setdefault(\\\"content\\\", {})[\\\"text/event-stream\\\"] = sse_content\\n                elif route_response_media_type:\\n                    response_schema = {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}\\n                    if lenient_issubclass(current_response_class, JSONResponse):\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/responses.py (hunk at line 1).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/responses.py\", \"old_text\": \"from typing import Any\\n\\nfrom fastapi.exceptions import FastAPIDeprecationWarning\\nfrom starlette.responses import FileResponse as FileResponse  # noqa\\nfrom starlette.responses import HTMLResponse as HTMLResponse  # noqa\\nfrom starlette.responses import JSONResponse as JSONResponse  # noqa\", \"new_text\": \"from typing import Any\\n\\nfrom fastapi.exceptions import FastAPIDeprecationWarning\\nfrom fastapi.sse import EventSourceResponse as EventSourceResponse  # noqa\\nfrom starlette.responses import FileResponse as FileResponse  # noqa\\nfrom starlette.responses import HTMLResponse as HTMLResponse  # noqa\\nfrom starlette.responses import JSONResponse as JSONResponse  # noqa\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_15030", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "48d58ae3b6ef4ded5a4794618c00345667256d98", "files": ["docs_src/server_sent_events/tutorial001_py310.py", "docs_src/server_sent_events/tutorial002_py310.py", "docs_src/server_sent_events/tutorial003_py310.py", "docs_src/server_sent_events/tutorial004_py310.py", "docs_src/server_sent_events/tutorial005_py310.py", "fastapi/openapi/utils.py", "fastapi/responses.py", "fastapi/routing.py", "fastapi/sse.py"], "symbols": ["Item", "sse_items", "sse_items_no_async", "sse_items_no_annotation"], "n_hunks": 17, "n_files": 9, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 6, "test_target": ["tests/test_sse.py", "tests/test_tutorial/test_server_sent_events/test_tutorial001.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "patch_context", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are patch_context.", "turns": 29, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 15, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1913, "split_from": "fastapi_15030"}}
