ore attempting to get its length.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/moto/cognitoidp/models.py\", \"old_text\": \"self.scopes = scopes\", \"new_text\": \"self.scopes = scopes if scopes is not None else []\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [str_replace_editor]:\nThe file /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/moto/cognitoidp/models.py has been edited. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/moto/cognitoidp/models.py:\n   899\t    ):\n   900\t        self.user_pool_id = user_pool_id\n   901\t        self.identifier = identifier\n   902\t        self.name = name\n   903\t        self.scopes = scopes if scopes is not None else []\n   904\t\n   905\t    def to_json(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n   906\t        res: Dict[str, Any] = {\n   907\t            \"UserPoolId\": self.user_pool_id,\nReview the changes and make sure they are as expected. Edit the file again if necessary."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/moto/cognitoidp/models.py\", \"old_text\": \"if len(self.scopes) != 0:\", \"new_text\": \"if self.scopes:\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [str_replace_editor]:\nThe file /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/moto/cognitoidp/models.py has been edited. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/moto/cognitoidp/models.py:\n   908\t            \"Identifier\": self.identifier,\n   909\t            \"Name\": self.name,\n   910\t        }\n   911\t\n   912\t        if self.scopes:\n   913\t            res.update({\"Scopes\": self.scopes})\n   914\t\n   915\t        return res\n   916\t\nReview the changes and make sure they are as expected. Edit the file again if necessary."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"pat