type: \"int\")\r\nFound 1 error in 1 file (checked 1 source file)[Python Interpreter: /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/bin/python]\nroot@openhands-workspace:/workspace/python__mypy__0.820 # \n[Command finished with exit code 1]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The error still persists, indicating that the change did not resolve the issue. It seems that the logic adjustment was not sufficient to address the problem. Let's take a closer look at the logic and consider additional modifications.\n\n### Further Investigation:\n- We need to ensure that the logic correctly handles `Optional` types when `strict_optional` is disabled.\n- Consider additional conditions or adjustments to the logic that might be necessary to prevent the false positive.\n\nLet's revisit the logic and make further adjustments.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"read_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/python__mypy__0.820/mypy/checkexpr.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [str_replace_editor]:\nHere's the result of running `cat -n` on /workspace/python__mypy__0.820/mypy/checkexpr.py:\n  2350\t        if isinstance(left, LiteralType) and isinstance(right, LiteralType):\n  2351\t            if isinstance(left.value, bool) and isinstance(right.value, bool):\n  2352\t                # Comparing different booleans is not dangerous.\n  2353\t                return False\n  2354\t        return not is_overlapping_types(left, right, ignore_promotions=False)\n  2355\t\n  2356\t    def get_operator_method(self, op: str) -> str:\n  2357\t        if op == '/' and self.chk.options.python_version[0] == 2:\n  2358\t            # TODO also check for \"from __future__ import division\"\n  2359\t            return '__div__'\n  2360\t        else:\n  2361\t            return nodes.op_methods[op]\n  2362\t\n  2363\t    def check_method_call_by_name(self,\n  2364\t                                  method: str,\n  2365\t                                  base_type: Type,\n  2366