r\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n- [ ] New feature\r\n- [ ] Documentation / docstrings\r\n- [x] Tests\r\n- [ ] Other\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] I've run the latest [black](https://github.com/psf/black) with default args on new code.\r\n- [ ] I've updated CHANGELOG.md and CONTRIBUTORS.md where appropriate.\r\n- [x] I've added tests for new code.\r\n- [x] I accept that @willmcgugan may be pedantic in the code review.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nFixed the bug [#3327](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues/3327).\r\n\r\nChanges -\r\n1. Added '@' in rich.highlighter:ReprHighlighter url regex pattern.\r\n2. Added a test case in test_highlighter for the url with '@'.\r\n\r\n## Note\r\nPoetry installed black v22.12.0 and its formatting differs a bit from the latest version v24.8.0. Hence I've formatted with the prior to keep it consistent."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"ReprHighlighter\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"ReprHighlighter\",\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rich/highlighter.py\",\n   \"line\": 80,\n   \"kind\": \"definition\"\n  }\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "ReprHighlighter is defined in rich/highlighter.py. Checking its callers and callees before reading any file.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"ReprHighlighter\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"ReprHighlighter\",\n \"callers\": [],\n \"callees\": [],\n \"note\": \"neighbors derived from symbols co-occurring in the patch\"\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Getting the surrounding call graph so I read only the files that matter.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_subgraph\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"ReprHighlighter\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "ric