ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix support for `StreamingResponse`s with dependencies with `yield` or `UploadFile`s, close after the response is done\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix support for `StreamingResponse`s with dependencies with `yield` or `UploadFile`s, close after the response is done\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThere's (again) an `AsyncExitStack` middleware, now used mainly to close objects after the response is done.\r\n\r\nThere's also a new wrapper duplicating some logic in Starlette but creating an `AsyncExitStack` for the exit code in dependencies with `yield`, for regular responses and WebSockets as well.\r\n\r\nThe exit code of dependencies with `yield` is now executed after the response is done."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Reading fastapi/applications.py around the suspect symbol.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"read_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/applications.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "fastapi/applications.py (lines 17-166 of 4616):\n17| from fastapi.datastructures import Default, DefaultPlaceholder\n18| from fastapi.exception_handlers import (\n19|     http_exception_handler,\n20|     request_validation_exception_handler,\n21|     websocket_request_validation_exception_handler,\n22| )\n23| from fastapi.exceptions import RequestValidationError, WebSocketRequestValidationError\n24| from fastapi.logger import logger\n25| from fastapi.openapi.docs import (\n26|     get_redoc_html,\n27|     get_swagger_ui_html,\n28|     get_swagger_ui_oauth2_redirect_html,\n29| )\n30| from fastapi.openapi.utils import get_openapi\n31| from fastapi.params import Depends\n32| from fastapi.types import DecoratedCallable, IncEx\n33| from fastapi.utils import generate_unique_id\n34| from starlette.applications import Starlette\n35| from starlette.datastructures import State\n36| from starlette.exceptions import HTTPException\n37| from starlette.middleware import Middleware\n38| from starlette.middleware.base import BaseHTTPMiddleware\n39| from starlette.requests import Request\n40| from starlette.responses import HTMLResponse, JSONResponse, Response\n41| from starlette.routing import BaseRoute\n42| from starlette.types import ASGIApp, Lifespan, Receive, Scope, Send\n43| from typing_extensions import Annotated, Doc, deprecated\n44| \n45| AppType = TypeVar(\"AppType\", bound=\"FastAPI\")\n46| \n47| \n48| class FastAPI(Starlette):\n49|     \"\"\"\n50|     `FastAPI` app class, the main entrypoint to use FastAPI.\n51| \n52|     Read more in the\n53|     [FastAPI docs for First Steps](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/first-steps/).\n54| \n55|     ## Example\n56| \n57|     ```python\n58|     from fastapi import FastAPI\n59| \n60|     app = FastAPI()\n61|     ```\n62|     \"\"\"\n63| \n64|     def __init__(\n65|         self: AppType,\n66|         *,\n67|         debug: Annotated[\n68|             bool,\n69|             Doc(\n70|                 \"\"\"\n71|                 Boolean indicating if debug tracebacks should be returned on server\n72\n[... observation truncated ...]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_14099.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_14099 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom docs_src.dependencies.tutorial013_an_py310 import User  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix support for `StreamingResponse`s with dependencies with `yield` or `UploadFile`s, close after the response is done \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix support for `StreamingResponse`s with dependencies with `yield` or `Uploa...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", User)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File w